{:id "0030-lab-stage"
 :title "Lab staging: centred, upright letters on a stage that reads as 3D"
 :lupa/deps #{"0029-lab-renderer"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "The foreman's review of the first lab screenshots: everything works,
        but the letters on the left lean like italics even when settled
        (all their poses have zero rotation and wobble). The cause is the
        camera: it looks up at the text from below and off to one side, so
        perspective converges vertical strokes far from the image centre.
        The text also sits small in the top-left corner of an empty dark
        page, and nothing tells the eye there is depth. Stage it: the text
        block centred under the camera, letters upright at rest, larger
        type, and a faint stage floor so depth reads as intended."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/render.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
         "public/lab/index.html" "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "Presentation only; the pure core decides nothing new.
          - Camera: its axis passes through the centre of the text block, it
            pitches at most 8 degrees, and its field of view is modest
            (35-45 degrees), so a settled glyph's vertical edges lean by
            less than 2 degrees anywhere in the block.
          - Composition: the renderer centres the block (from the extent of
            the live poses' base layout, i.e. their x/y) horizontally and
            places it a little above the vertical centre of the viewport; it
            follows the block smoothly as lines are added (ease, no jumps).
            The type size fills about 70% of the viewport width at the
            layout width main.cljs chooses (pick width-em so a line is a
            comfortable 30-45 characters).
          - Depth: a faint stage floor below the text (a plane receding
            into the distance with fine lines or a soft gradient, in the
            ink palette, low contrast, aria-hidden like the canvas) and a
            gentle fog so letters further back (higher z) are dimmer. No
            new effects; z motion should simply read now.
          - Expose window.__lab.lean(i): the angle in degrees between the
            projected left edge of live glyph i's quad (bottom-left to
            top-left corners, through the instance matrix, camera and
            viewport) and the screen vertical.
          e2e/lab.mjs: after the settled step, assert |lean(i)| < 2 for
          every live glyph, and that the projected centre of the text block
          is within 12% of the viewport width of the horizontal centre.
          Keep every existing step. docs/LAB.md: a line on the staging."
 :acceptance
 ["`bb lab:e2e` passes with the new lean and centring assertions, and the
   final message lists the screenshots (the foreman will look at them)"
  "`bb test` stays green; nothing outside the scope changes"]
 :non-goals
 ["No changes to lab.draft, lab.cues, lab.pose, the glossary, or the
   schema; no new word effects; no sending yet"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/lab/render.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
           "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md" "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc"]
 :budget-usd 10.0}
